   "": {
    "actClause": "AN ACT to amend the New York city charter, in relation to notification by the New York city board of standards and appeals to certain affected state senators and assembly members",
    "basePrintNo": "S5050",
    "basePrintNoStr": "S5050-2015",
    "coSponsors": {
     "items": [],
     "size": 0
    },
    "fullText": "",
    "fullTextFormats": [],
    "fullTextHtml": "",
    "fullTextTemplate": "",
    "lawCode": "Amd §§196, 197-b, 200 & 201, NYC Chart",
    "lawSection": "New York City Charter",
    "memo": "BILL NUMBER:S5050\n\nTITLE OF BILL:  An act to amend the New York city charter, in relation\nto notification by the New York city board of standards and appeals to\ncertain affected state senators and assembly members\n\nPURPOSE OR GENERAL IDEA OF BILL:  The purpose of the bill is to\nprovide notice to affected state elected officials of applications to\nthe New York City board of standards and appeals.\n\nSUMMARY OF PROVISIONS:\n\nSection 1 of the bill amends section 196 of the New York City charter\nto include \"affected senator or assembly member\", which shall mean the\nrespective senator or assembly member for the land included in a plan\nor application.\n\nSection 2 amends section 197-b, subdivision a, to require the affected\nsenator or assembly member receive advance notice of all preliminary\nand final plans of public agencies and public benefit corporations, or\nof private agencies, entities or developers filed with the city, that\nrelate to the use, development or improvement of land subject to city\nregulation.\n\nSubdivision b is amended to require that copies of all requests for\nproposals and other solicitations of proposals issued by or on behalf\nof the city, and all letters of intent executed by or on behalf of the\ncity, shall also be conveyed to the affected senator or assembly\nmember where such land is located.\n\nSection 3 amends subdivision a of section 200 of the New York City\ncharter to provide that before the city planning commission amends the\ntext of a zoning resolution, the commission shall also notify the\naffected senator or assembly member and afford those interested an\nopportunity to be heard.\n\nSection 4 amends subdivision a of section 201 of the New York City\ncharter to provide that before adopting any applications for changes\nin the zoning resolutions and regulations, the commission will refer\nthem to the affected senators or assembly members for a public hearing\nand recommendation.\n\nSection 5 provides that this act shall take effect immediately.\n\nJUSTIFICATION:  While the New York City charter currently requires\nthat the affected community board and borough president receive\nnotification of applications to the board of standards and appeals,\nthe affected state senator and assembly members are not included.\nHowever, it is critical that\n\nPRIOR LEGISLATIVE HISTORY:  None.\n\nFISCAL IMPLICATIONS FOR STATE AND LOCAL GOVERNMENTS:  None\n\nEFFECTIVE DATE:  This act shall take effect immediately.\n\n\n",
